Thank you Murray,

Ok, we'll try moving locations/points so that they fall inside the plot boundaries but will reject those that are "way" outside the plot. There is still an arbitrary aspect to which ones we adjust and which ones we discard but might have to live with it. We are looking into antennas that will increase the accuracy of the GPS so we'll see.

Good point on the edge effects being greater on the smaller plots than the larger colony area. The population trends shown by the data are pretty much the same for SECR and MARK estimates but with SECR can get an estimate for the whole colony. However this might have been biased because we expanded the plot dimensions. We'll try the GPS point adjustments and see how that goes.

thank you!

Scott

