OK, but you don't make it easy. I'm not clear whether we're dealing with one error or two. A trap covariate should not work in models for phi. You appear to have covariates with many levels - these can slow things down and demand extra space.  Size alone should not cause the errors, unless the product of the dimensions of an internal array gets ridiculous.

 Certainly openCR should not crash R - I can debug  given a minimal example that fails (my own example works).
There's plenty you can do to make your own tests - drop HHR and BVT for a start.

You have an extra comma in your code near the end.

